menu "Yaykit TF card"

config YK_TF_READ_ONLY
    bool "The card is read-only (test bench)"
    default n
    help
        The disk under FatFs has no way to write, and no directory is made: for shared-test, which looks at cards that
        may hold someone's old recordings. Never in a firmware that ships.

config YK_TF_SYSTEM
    bool "The system's side of the card (Yay, shared-test)"
    default n
    select FATFS_USE_LABEL
    help
        sys_include/yk_tf_sys.h and yk_tf_pkg.h: the system area, the store of app images and 形象 packs, the index in
        NVS. Only the main firmware and the test bench, which also put sys_include/ on their include path; never an
        app, and the kit has none of it (Yay 0.1.19 开发文档 6.1). Without it the card still cleans up after a power
        cut, measures an app's space and stops before deep sleep. It turns on FatFs's volume label: the system names
        a card that has no name TIKPAL (4.2).

endmenu
